---
import { BRAND, FRAMEWORK_NAMES, PHP_MIN_VERSION, PRODUCT_NAME, WIRING_PARTS } from '../../consts/product';
import { LINKS } from '../../consts/site';
import { SNIPPETS } from '../../consts/snippets';
import { capitalize, inline, listOf, numberWord } from '../../lib/format';
import Actions from '../Actions.astro';
import Button from '../Button.astro';
import CodeCard from '../CodeCard.astro';
import Row from '../Row.astro';
import RuleList from '../RuleList.astro';
import Section from '../Section.astro';
import Stack from '../Stack.astro';
---

<Section id="get-started" heading="Getting started">
  <div>
    <Row>
      <h3 slot="label" class="t-title">1. Get your license</h3>
      <p class="t-body measure">
        {PRODUCT_NAME} is an advanced extension of {BRAND}, released under a commercial license.
        <a href={LINKS.contact}>Talk to us</a> to get yours: it gives your team access to the package, with the details to add
        it to your projects through Composer.
      </p>
    </Row>
    <Row>
      <h3 slot="label" class="t-title">2. Install the package</h3>
      <Stack>
        <p class="t-body">Once your project has access, install it like any other Composer package:</p>
        <CodeCard title="Terminal" snippet={SNIPPETS.install} />
        <p class="t-body">
          It requires PHP {PHP_MIN_VERSION} or later and an application that already uses
          <a href={LINKS.neuronGithub}>{BRAND}</a>.
        </p>
      </Stack>
    </Row>
    <Row>
      <h3 slot="label" class="t-title">3. Wire it in</h3>
      <Stack>
        <p class="t-body">
          {capitalize(numberWord(WIRING_PARTS.length))} parts, all built the same way in every process of your application.
        </p>
        <RuleList>
          {WIRING_PARTS.map((part) => <li set:html={inline(part)} />)}
        </RuleList>
        <CodeCard title="background.php" snippet={SNIPPETS.bootstrap} />
        <CodeCard title="SupportAgent.php" snippet={SNIPPETS.agent} />
        <CodeCard title="PHP" snippet={SNIPPETS.serve} />
        <CodeCard title="crontab" snippet={SNIPPETS.cron} />
        <p class="t-body">
          That's the whole setup for a plain PHP application. On {listOf(FRAMEWORK_NAMES)}, the integration packages do it for
          you.
        </p>
        <Actions>
          <Button href={LINKS.contact}>Talk to us</Button>
        </Actions>
      </Stack>
    </Row>
  </div>
</Section>
